# BW-2001 (Machine 130): the PET 2001's board 320137. Every chip at its PET location (grid pet,
# P5q): rows A (back) to J (front), columns 1 (left) to 9 (right). The edge connectors at the
# back as on the PET, the monitor and cassette #1 at the left, the keyboard at the front.
grid pet
edge J3 back 10%
edge J2 back 40%
edge J1 back 75%
edge J6 left back
edge J7 left 60%
edge J5 front middle
edge J8 right front
edge DS1 right 30%

# Pull-ups beside the chip whose pins they hold (the schematic's), chained along a row.
next R28 UE2 front              # BA0
next R29 UE3 front              # BA1-BA5
next R30 R29 right
next R31 R30 right
next R32 R31 right
next R33 R32 right
next R34 R33 right              # BA6-BA10, on along the same row
next R35 R34 right
next R36 R35 right
next R37 R36 right
next R38 R37 right
next R21 UG8 front              # KIN0-KIN7, the keyboard columns, both ways from the middle
next R20 R21 left
next R19 R20 left
next R18 R19 left
next R22 R21 right
next R23 R22 right
next R24 R23 right
next R25 R24 right
next R10 UA9 front              # IFC_N, EOI_N
next R48 R10 right
next R13 UF3 front              # NMI_N, RDY, IRQ_N
next R14 R13 right
next R17 R14 right
next R26 UG3 front              # spare inputs of UG3, UG4
next R46 UE2 back               # the clock gate's enable
next R12 UC7 front              # the flip-flops' J, K and clears
next R39 UC5 front
next R40 UD2 front
next R41 UB6 front
next R43 UA1 front
next R44 UC1 front
next R45 R44 right
next R27 UE8 front
